===Etymology===
From {{confix|en|haemo|philia}}, from {{uder|en|grc|αἷμα|t=[[blood]]}} + {{m|grc|φιλία|t=[[friendship]]}}. Originally called [[haemorrhaphilia]], probably from the word [[haemorrhage]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌhiːməˈfɪliə, -ˈfiːliə/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-haemophilia.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-haemophilia.wav|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪliə|s=5}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːliə}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|British spelling|pathology}} Any of several hereditary illnesses that impair the body's ability to control bleeding, usually passed from mother to son.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|bleeder's disease}}
* {{l|en|bleeding sickness}}
* {{l|en|Christmas disease}}

